From 508014e752e10050713f86360439c8743876239c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:01:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): deduplicate board-qualified local closeout
 obligations [daveey]

Problem: a chat whose settled batch holds a human-blocked local card painted it twice: kanban_blocked=1 AND
kanban_active=1 (grey + red), kanban_waiting_on=['default/t_b','t_b']. Reproduced with the real chat-closeout
core.card_key over core's session_tasks rows.

Why 1: annotate_kanban_activity added the closeout key 'default/t_b' to kanban_active because it matched neither
open_ids nor the counted card keys.
Why 2: open_ids are bare task ids ('t_b'); the snapshot's local card keys were '<db path>/<tid>'
(kanban_activity_identity.local_keys), while chat-closeout's card_key emits '<board slug>/<tid>' for local cards
(the same form core's parked_waits uses).
Why 3: the local key was introduced only for lineage dedup, where any unique label works; the remote fix
(5e059f005f3) reused the merged key set for closeout dedup without aligning the local label.
Root (happened): two local-identity formats for one card with no shared contract.
Root (not caught): the core closeout test fed bare ids ('t1'), not the plugin's board-qualified form.

Fix: local keys are '<board slug>/<tid>' (slugs have no '/', remote keys have >= 3 parts, so local and remote
never collide; different boards stay distinct). A counted local card's scoped closeout alias is dropped from
kanban_waiting_on (it is listed under its bare id). waiting_on_task_ids() is unchanged (bare ids).

Tests: test_kanban_local_waiting_overlap.py (plugin key format via session_tasks; running/review/human-blocked/
triage overlaps, unrelated closeouts, same id on another board, named board, legacy bare ids, mixed local+remote,
lineage dedup across boards, waiting_on_task_ids API). RED on main: 10 failed; GREEN: all pass.
---
